IMPORT prelude

-- Feeding Stuffs Act 1965 (Singapore) -- what the Act decides for a person or business dealing in animal feed: the licence to
-- import, manufacture, process for sale or sell (s 4), the seller's statutory statement (s 5), the manufacturer's warranty (s 6), the
-- purchaser's right to a sample and analysis (s 7), arrest without warrant (s 8(3)), the privilege against self-incrimination in
-- an investigation (s 8A(2)), the offences and their maxima (ss 4(5), 10), and the ceiling on penalties in rules (s 11(3)(b)).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/FSA1965.txt. The deposit says the revised edition
-- "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021"; the latest
-- amendment annotated in the body is [11/2019] (the Singapore Food Agency Act 2019). The retrieval metadata calls it the current
-- version as at 1 October 2026. NOTE: the ARRANGEMENT OF SECTIONS at the top of the deposit is out of step by one (it pairs "2." with
-- "Short title" and so on); this encoding follows the section numbers in the BODY.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0089 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl: tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. It asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a sharper
-- question yet. The Act is short (11 sections), so the scope is nearly all of it. Not encoded: administration and appointment of
-- authorised officers (s 3), entry and inspection powers (s 8(1), (2)) beyond their effect on the s 10(6) offence, the s 8A
-- investigation procedure beyond s 8A(2), payment of fees to the Agency (s 9), and the rule-making power (s 11) beyond the penalty
-- ceiling. No rules made under s 11 were retrieved, so every "prescribed" form, particular and fee is unknown here.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text, following the conventions of the example rows (the writing-l4-rules skill was
-- not available in this session). No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Feeding Stuffs Act 1965 -- feeds and dealings`

-- s 2: "animal feed" means "organic or mineral substances or mixtures of such substances used for the feeding of animals".
-- "simple feed" means a livestock feed "declared by the Minister, by notification in the Gazette, to be a simple feed"; "feed
-- concentrate" supplements or balances a feed ratio "and includes mineral mixtures"; "compound feed" affords "the full range of
-- nutritional ingredients". Any other animal feed (for example a livestock feed never gazetted as a simple feed) is an animal feed
-- but none of the three named kinds.
DECLARE Feed IS ONE OF
    `a simple feed`
    `a feed concentrate`
    `a compound feed`
    `another animal feed`

DECLARE Dealing IS ONE OF
    `importing`
    `manufacturing`
    `processing for sale`
    `selling`
    `buying`
    `storing for own animals`

-- The three named kinds recur throughout ss 4, 6, 8(1)(a), 10(4) and 10(6). The label "a named feed" is this encoding's, not the Act's.
GIVEN `the feed` IS A Feed
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a named feed` IF
    CONSIDER `the feed`
    WHEN `another animal feed` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `4 -- licence to import, manufacture, process for sale or sell`

-- s 4(4): "No person shall import, manufacture, process for sale or sell simple feeds, feed concentrates or compound feeds without a
-- licence issued by the Director-General." (5): contravention is an offence, "a fine not exceeding $1,000 or ... imprisonment for a
-- term not exceeding 12 months or ... both". (3): the Director-General "may, in his discretion, at any time, revoke or suspend a
-- licence." The Act gives no criteria for revocation and no appeal.
GIVEN `the dealing` IS A Dealing
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a licensable dealing` IF
    CONSIDER `the dealing`
    WHEN `importing` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `manufacturing` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `processing for sale` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `selling` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the dealing` IS A Dealing, `the feed` IS A Feed
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a licence is needed` IF
    `is a licensable dealing` `the dealing` AND `is a named feed` `the feed`

-- A licence suspended or revoked under s 4(3) is treated as no licence (inference: the text does not say so in terms).
GIVEN `the dealing` IS A Dealing, `the feed` IS A Feed, `holds a licence in force` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `dealing without a licence is an offence` IF
    `a licence is needed` `the dealing` `the feed` AND (NOT `holds a licence in force`)

§§ `5 and 10(1) -- the seller's statutory statement`

-- s 5: "Every person who sells animal feeds shall furnish to the purchaser on or before delivery or as soon as possible a written
-- statement in the prescribed form". It covers ANY animal feed, not only the three named kinds. (The arrangement and the heading call
-- it an obligation "by purchaser"; the text puts it on the seller.) s 10(1): failure is an offence, $1,000 or 12 months or both.
-- "As soon as possible" is not modelled as a deadline; the case states whether the statement was furnished.
GIVEN `sold animal feed` IS A BOOLEAN, `furnished the statement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `failing to furnish the statement is an offence` IF
    `sold animal feed` AND (NOT `furnished the statement`)

§§ `6 and 10(2), (3) -- the manufacturer's warranty`

-- s 6: "A manufacturer of simple feeds, feed concentrates or compound feeds shall give to every purchaser a warranty in the
-- prescribed form". s 10(2): a manufacturer "who does not supply a warranty" commits an offence; (3): so does one "who furnishes a
-- warranty containing statements that are incorrect or inaccurate". Neither offence has a mental element in the text.
GIVEN `the feed` IS A Feed, `is the manufacturer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a warranty is due` IF
    `is the manufacturer` AND `is a named feed` `the feed`

GIVEN `the feed` IS A Feed, `is the manufacturer` IS A BOOLEAN, `gave a warranty` IS A BOOLEAN, `the warranty is inaccurate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a warranty offence is committed` IF
        `a warranty is due` `the feed` `is the manufacturer`
    AND (    (NOT `gave a warranty`)
         OR  (`gave a warranty` AND `the warranty is inaccurate`))

§§ `7 -- the purchaser's right to a sample and analysis`

-- s 7: "The purchaser of any animal feed shall on payment of the prescribed fees be entitled to -- (a) have a sample of the article
-- taken by an authorised officer and analysed; and (b) receive a certificate of the result of the analysis."
GIVEN `bought animal feed` IS A BOOLEAN, `paid the prescribed fee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the purchaser is entitled to a sample and certificate` IF
    `bought animal feed` AND `paid the prescribed fee`

§§ `10(4) -- deleterious ingredients`

-- s 10(4): where a simple feed, feed concentrate or compound feed "which has been sold" is "found on analysis to contain any
-- ingredient deleterious or dangerous to animals, the seller, manufacturer or proprietor, as the case may be, shall be DEEMED to be
-- guilty of an offence". No knowledge, fault or defence appears in the text. The offence is limited to the three named kinds: a
-- deleterious "other" animal feed falls outside it.
GIVEN `the feed` IS A Feed, `was sold` IS A BOOLEAN, `analysis found a deleterious ingredient` IS A BOOLEAN, `knew of it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the seller is deemed guilty` IF
    `is a named feed` `the feed` AND `was sold` AND `analysis found a deleterious ingredient`

§§ `10(5), (6) -- tampering and obstruction`

-- s 10(5): an offence to "(a) fraudulently tamper with any animal feed so as to procure that any sample ... does not correctly
-- represent the article; or (b) tamper or interfere with any sample submitted for analysis". (a) needs fraud; (b) does not.
GIVEN `tampered with the feed` IS A BOOLEAN, `fraudulently, so the sample misrepresents it` IS A BOOLEAN, `tampered with a submitted sample` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a tampering offence is committed` IF
        (`tampered with the feed` AND `fraudulently, so the sample misrepresents it`)
    OR  `tampered with a submitted sample`

-- s 10(6): "Any owner of, or person entrusted for the time being with the charge and custody of, simple feeds, feed concentrates or
-- compound feeds who -- (a) refuses to allow any authorised officer to take samples as he thinks fit; or (b) otherwise WILFULLY
-- delays or obstructs any authorised officer". s 8(2) lets an officer sample ANY animal feed, but the refusal offence names only the
-- three kinds.
GIVEN `the feed` IS A Feed, `is owner or custodian` IS A BOOLEAN, `refused sampling` IS A BOOLEAN, `wilfully obstructed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an obstruction offence is committed` IF
        `is owner or custodian` AND `is a named feed` `the feed`
    AND (`refused sampling` OR `wilfully obstructed`)

§§ `4(5), 10 and 11(3)(b) -- maximum penalties`

-- Every offence in the Act (ss 4(5), 10(1) to (6)) carries the same maximum: "a fine not exceeding $1,000 or ... imprisonment for a
-- term not exceeding 12 months or ... both". s 11(3)(b): rules may impose penalties not exceeding "a fine of $500 or imprisonment for
-- a term of 6 months or both", and (c) may add cancellation or suspension of a licence.
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `an offence under the Act`
    `an offence under rules`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `an offence under the Act` THEN 1000
    WHEN `an offence under rules` THEN 500

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `an offence under the Act` THEN 12
    WHEN `an offence under rules` THEN 6

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `licence cancellation may be added` IF
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `an offence under rules` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `8(3), (4) -- arrest without warrant`

-- s 8(3): the Director-General or an authorised officer "may arrest without warrant" a person committing, attempting, or reasonably
-- suspected of committing or attempting an offence, IF "(a) the person refuses to furnish his name and address or furnishes an address
-- out of Singapore; or (b) there are reasonable grounds for believing that the person has furnished a false name or address or ... is
-- likely to abscond." (4): the person must be brought before a Magistrate's Court "without unnecessary delay".
GIVEN `suspected of an offence` IS A BOOLEAN, `refused name and address` IS A BOOLEAN, `gave an address out of Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN, `false name or address suspected` IS A BOOLEAN, `likely to abscond` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `arrest without warrant is allowed` IF
        `suspected of an offence`
    AND (   `refused name and address`
         OR `gave an address out of Singapore`
         OR `false name or address suspected`
         OR `likely to abscond`)

§§ `8A(2) -- answering questions`

-- s 8A(2): a person examined "is bound to state truly the facts and circumstances ... except only that the person may decline to
-- make ... a statement which would have a tendency to expose the person to a criminal charge or to penalty or forfeiture."
GIVEN `tends to expose to a charge, penalty or forfeiture` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person may decline to answer` IF
    `tends to expose to a charge, penalty or forfeiture`
